<title>MEXICO: Japan to loan $200 mln to Mexican state for sewage.</title>
<headline>Japan to loan $200 mln to Mexican state for sewage.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan has agreed to issue a long-term $200 million credit to the western Mexican state of Jalisco for sewage treatment in Mexico's third largest city of Guadalajara, an official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Jose Levy, minister of finances in Jalisco, said a letter of intent had been signed between the governments of both countries, and that the loan would be signed in August.</p>
<p>The funds would go toward construction of a sewage treatment plant for Guadalajara, to avoid the dumping of polluted waste waters in rivers in Jalisco.</p>
<p>Levy has previously said the yen loan would have a 25-year maturity, with seven years grace, and that interest would be three percent a year.</p>
<p>(--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397)</p>
